hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1608","Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala narrated to us, and he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq. And Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, and he said: Salamah narrated to us, and he narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Ishaq. And Bundar narrated to us, and he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, and he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, and he narrated to me from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Mutarrif, who said: I entered upon Uthman ibn Abi al-As (RA), so he said: The last instruction the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave me when he appointed me over Ta'if was: \O Uthman"," shorten the prayer"," and accommodate the congregation according to the capacity of their weakest members"," for among them are the elderly"," the frail"," the sick"," and those with pressing needs.\"""""
